# ◈ packages.graphics.list — graphics / display stack
#
# ASSUMPTION (flag if wrong): Wayland-minimal, not Xorg. Rationale — AthanorOS
# is already non-systemd/musl/llvm and minimalism-first.
#
# CORRECTED from an earlier revision: dropped gui-apps/cage — it's not in
# the main Gentoo tree (Gentoo's own Wayland software list confirms several
# kiosk-style wlroots compositors only live in the GURU overlay), and
# packages.desktop.list's gui-wm/sway now covers the "usable live
# environment" goal that cage was originally meant for. If a pure kiosk
# mode is wanted later, that's an overlay-enablement step to add
# deliberately, not something to pull in by accident.
#
# Also dropped sys-libs/libseat as its own atom — it isn't a separate
# Gentoo package. The libseat client library ships as part of
# sys-auth/seatd itself (confirmed: seatd already builds fine on its own).
#
# `seatd` replaces systemd-logind/elogind for seat and session management
# (VT switching, device access) without pulling in either systemd or the
# elogind compatibility shim — matches the existing OpenRC-only design.
#
# If you'd rather target Xorg instead (more battle-tested with older
# Calamares/KPMcore releases, heavier stack): swap this file's wayland/wlroots
# entries for xorg-server + xf86-input-libinput + a minimal WM, and drop
# qtwayland from packages.kde-qt.list.

media-libs/mesa                   use:llvm,wayland,vulkan,-X
x11-libs/libdrm
x11-libs/pixman
media-libs/libglvnd
media-libs/vulkan-loader
dev-libs/wayland
dev-libs/wayland-protocols
gui-libs/wlroots
sys-auth/seatd
media-libs/fontconfig
media-libs/freetype
media-fonts/noto
